    "state": "COMMENTED",
    "body": "Extracting `runningInstanceLines` as a pure function is the right move — inline in the command action this branch could only be exercised by launching a detached server, which is why the gap survived #358 in the first place.\n\n`getOptionValueSource(\"port\") === \"cli\"` is the correct predicate, and the comment explains why the obvious alternative is wrong in *both* directions: comparing against the default stays silent for someone who explicitly typed `-p 8080` against a server running elsewhere (exactly the case they typed the flag to discover), and nags anyone who typed nothing.\n\nThe `runningPort === null` test earns its place — asserting that no `http://localhost` appears at all is a direct regression guard on the confidently-wrong URL #358 removed. Easy to reintroduce that through a new warning path; now it fails loudly.\n\n`status` reporting the URL is the small one that will get used the most.\n\nAll checks green. Approving.\n",
